{"uncertainty": 0.3, "outcome": "A new self-checking SystemVerilog testbench, irq_ctrl_cov_tb.sv, is provided for the platform's coverage.read run over the approved irq_ctrl.v. A coverage_report artifact describes the stimulus plan and one design point that no stimulus can reach. No coverage numbers are reported because no coverage run has happened yet.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "coverage_report", "title": "irq_ctrl coverage plan and reachability analysis (pre-run, no measured numbers)", "summary": "Coverage plan for the approved RTL [artifact:prj-63d6b8e26c.design-under-test.a1], serving [requirement:req-1e26d9c190]. It replaces the approved idle testbench [artifact:prj-63d6b8e26c.testbench.a1]. That testbench passed 5 checks in [run:run-0001] [evidence:prj-63d6b8e26c.testbench.e1], but by its own header it never raises a source, so detection, claim and acknowledge never run. The new testbench builds the DUT with N=32, the largest size the RTL allows. With N=8, rdata[30:8], rdata[4:3] and irq_id[4:3] are fixed at zero by construction and their toggle points could never be hit, so those gaps would not be justified holes. With N=32 every register bit drives a port. Stimulus, by design point: (1) full-width writes and readback of ENABLE (all ones, all zeros, A5A5A5A5, 5A5A5A5A) and MODE, and an all-ones write to PENDING; this toggles wdata, enable, mode, w1c and rdata. (2) Level-mode detection on all 32 sources, then a claim/acknowledge sweep from source 0 to 31 that checks irq_id and the CLAIM read at each step; this toggles detect, pending, active, ack, ack_hit, irq, irq_id and rdata[4:0] and rdata[31]. (3) An edge-mode rising edge on all sources, followed by holding the sources high and clearing them; this checks that a held source does not trigger again. (4) A detection beating a clear on the same edge, in both edge and level mode. (5) Enable masking and priority among a subset of sources. A CLAIM write with wdata[31:5] nonzero must acknowledge only wdata[4:0], and an acknowledge of a non-pending source must have no effect. (6) A reset in mid-test with sources held high, which gives the 1-to-0 toggle on rst_n and covers the reset branch, followed by a check on source 31. Unreachable point: wire unused_wdata = &{1'b0, wdata} is always 0, so its toggle point cannot be hit. It is justified as unreachable by construction and is not excluded with a pragma. The integer i is outside Verilator toggle coverage. Measured line and toggle percentages, and any further uncovered points, can come only from the platform's coverage.read run."}], "files": [{"path": "irq_ctrl_cov_tb.sv", "kind": "testbench", "title": "irq_ctrl_cov_tb.sv: self-checking coverage testbench for irq_ctrl (N=32)", "summary": "Self-checking testbench for the approved RTL [artifact:prj-63d6b8e26c.design-under-test.a1], written for [requirement:req-1e26d9c190]. It extends the approach of [artifact:prj-63d6b8e26c.testbench.a1] and keeps its verdict format: a single NIRMAAN-SIM line carrying the nonce plusarg. It exercises register readback, level and edge detection, W1C clearing, a full fixed-priority claim/acknowledge sweep over 32 sources, the rule that a detection beats a clear, enable masking, ignored upper wdata bits on acknowledge, and a mid-test reset. It contains no $fopen, $system, $c, DPI, include, Verilator configuration or coverage pragma.", "entry": "irq_ctrl_cov_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["The testbench is expected to pass all its checks on the approved irq_ctrl.v; this has not been run.", "Line coverage of irq_ctrl.v is expected to reach every statement, including both reset branches, both register-write conditions, every case arm and the priority loop; not measured.", "Toggle coverage is expected to miss only the constant wire unused_wdata, about 1 of roughly 365 bit points at N=32; not measured.", "Branch percentages, if any are reported, come from whatever points the line/toggle build produces and were not targeted separately."], "escalation": null, "notes": "The DUT is instantiated with N=32 rather than the default N=8. This is deliberate: at N=8 about 28 toggle points on rdata and irq_id are tied to zero by the RTL, so they would cap toggle coverage near 82% whatever the stimulus. If the requirement's coverage targets must be met at N=8 specifically, that needs a decision from verification.dynamic.coverage.code.senior, because those points would then need written unreachable justifications. Every input changes 1 ns after a rising clock edge to avoid races with the sampling edge. Each check prints a MISMATCH line on failure, in addition to the single verdict line."}
